Experiment: Jenkins Installation and Setup – Explore the Environment
Aim
To install Jenkins, set up the Jenkins environment, and create a simple build job.
Requirements
Hardware:
RAM: 4 GB
Hard disk: More than 50 GB
Software:
JDK or JRE
Web Browser
Ubuntu Operating System
RECORD 27 dev (1).pdf
Procedure
Step 1: Install Jenkins
Add the Jenkins repository and update the system.
sudo apt update

sudo apt install jenkins
Step 2: Start Jenkins
Start the Jenkins server using:
sudo systemctl start jenkins
Check the status:
sudo systemctl status jenkins
Step 3: Open Jenkins
Open the browser and enter:
http://your_server_ip_or_domain:8080
Jenkins opens on its default port 8080. RECORD 27 dev (1).pdf
Step 4: Unlock Jenkins
Get the initial administrator password using:
sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword
Copy the password and paste it into the Jenkins setup page.
Step 5: Complete Setup
Click Install Suggested Plugins.
Create the first admin user.
Confirm the server address.
Click Save and Finish.
Click Start using Jenkins.


